/grid /arcade 301
/grid/* /arcade/:splat 301

# /ideas/ IS NOT SERVED WHILE AN ADSENSE REVIEW IS OPEN.
#
# The board is built and tested (supabase/92_ideas_board.sql, and ideas/ in commit 7479e737)
# but 92 has not been run, so what a visitor got at runthe.gg/ideas/ was a heading and the
# sentence "The ideas board is not set up on this project yet." A broken feature page is the
# worst thing a reviewer can land on, so the two files were taken out of the deployed tree.
#
# THIS RULE IS THE SECOND LOCK, not the first. Cloudflare's own docs are unreachable from
# the sandbox this was written in, so whether _redirects wins over a matching static asset
# could not be verified, and a guess is not good enough when being wrong means a rejection.
# The files being absent is what actually keeps the path empty; this catches the case where
# somebody restores them before the review closes.
#
# NOT robots.txt Disallow, which was the other idea and is worse: robots.txt is public, so a
# Disallow line advertises the path to exactly the reviewer it is meant to hide it from.
#
# TO TURN THE BOARD ON: run supabase/92_ideas_board.sql, restore the page with
#   git checkout 7479e737 -- ideas/
# delete these two lines, and read the comment at the top of ideas/index.html about what has
# to be true before it can be indexed or carry ads.
/ideas /404.html 404
/ideas/* /404.html 404
